IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc3-helpers`
IMPORT `ssc3-a-s43-s44`
IMPORT `ssc3-d-s47-s48c`

-- Tests for ssc3-d-s47-s48c.l4 (ss 47, 48, 48A, 48AA, 48B, 48BB, 48C).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section named beside it; none is copied from the encoding's output.
-- The fixtures' dates are chosen for the comparisons under test; a fixture is not a claim about when anyone really attains pensionable age (that is the keel's fact, ssc-core.l4).

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN `their sex` IS A Sex
      born IS A DATE
      attained IS A DATE
GIVETH A Person
`a person` MEANS
    Person WITH
        `date of birth` IS born
        `sex` IS `their sex`
        `marital status` IS `married`
        `date of attaining pensionable age` IS attained

`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2013` MEANS `a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1953) (Date 1 1 2013)
`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2013` MEANS `a person` Man (Date 1 1 1948) (Date 1 1 2013)
`a man born 6 April 1950 who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2015` MEANS `a person` Man (Date 6 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015)
`a man born 5 April 1950 who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2015` MEANS `a person` Man (Date 5 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015)
`a man born 1 January 1940 who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005` MEANS `a person` Man (Date 1 1 1940) (Date 1 1 2005)
`a man born 1 January 1949 who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2014` MEANS `a person` Man (Date 1 1 1949) (Date 1 1 2014)
`a woman born 1 January 1949 who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2009` MEANS `a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1949) (Date 1 1 2009)
`a woman born 1 January 1944 who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004` MEANS `a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1944) (Date 1 1 2004)
`a woman born 1 January 1955 who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2015` MEANS `a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1955) (Date 1 1 2015)

§ `Section 47: increase of Category A retirement pension for invalidity`

-- (6): 8 weeks, or a larger number of weeks specified in regulations.
#ASSERT `s 47(6) the number of weeks of subsection (1)` NOTHING EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `s 47(6) the number of weeks of subsection (1)` (JUST 12) EQUALS 12
-- (1)(a): the 8 weeks ending immediately before 6 April 2021 begin on 9 February 2021 (56 days earlier) and end on 5 April 2021.
#ASSERT `s 47(1)(a) the day falls within the period of weeks ending immediately before the day the pensioner attains pensionable age` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 6 4 2021)) (Date 9 2 2021) 8
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 47(1)(a) the day falls within the period of weeks ending immediately before the day the pensioner attains pensionable age` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 6 4 2021)) (Date 8 2 2021) 8))
#ASSERT `s 47(1)(a) the day falls within the period of weeks ending immediately before the day the pensioner attains pensionable age` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 6 4 2021)) (Date 5 4 2021) 8
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 47(1)(a) the day falls within the period of weeks ending immediately before the day the pensioner attains pensionable age` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 6 4 2021)) (Date 6 4 2021) 8))
-- (6): with 10 weeks the period begins on 26 January 2021.
#ASSERT `s 47(1)(a) the day falls within the period of weeks ending immediately before the day the pensioner attains pensionable age` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 6 4 2021)) (Date 26 1 2021) 10
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 47(1)(a) the day falls within the period of weeks ending immediately before the day the pensioner attains pensionable age` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 6 4 2021)) (Date 25 1 2021) 10))
-- (1)(b): the last day before the beginning of that period.
#ASSERT `s 47(1)(b) the last day before the beginning of the period` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 6 4 2021)) 8 EQUALS Date 8 2 2021
#ASSERT `s 47(1)(b) the last day before the beginning of the period` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 6 4 2021)) 10 EQUALS Date 25 1 2021
-- (1): the increase is the age addition's rate when the pensioner was entitled on a day in the period or on the last day before it; section 61 takes it away.
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the increase of the weekly rate in pounds` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST 5.75) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the increase of the weekly rate in pounds` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST 5.75) EQUALS JUST 5.75
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the increase of the weekly rate in pounds` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST 5.75) EQUALS JUST 5.75
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the increase of the weekly rate in pounds` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST 5.75) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the increase of the weekly rate in pounds` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST 5.75) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the increase of the weekly rate in pounds` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST 5.75) EQUALS JUST 5.75
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the increase of the weekly rate in pounds` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the increase of the weekly rate in pounds` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST 5.75) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the increase of the weekly rate in pounds` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST 5.75) EQUALS JUST 0
-- (3A): additional pension for (2) and (3) leaves out the amount attributable to units of additional pension. 20 - 5 = 15.
#ASSERT `s 47(3A) the additional pension for subsections (2) and (3) in pounds` 20 5 EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `s 47(3A) the additional pension for subsections (2) and (3) in pounds` 20 0 EQUALS 20
-- (4): the additional pension after any increase under section 52(3) but without any increase under paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 5. 22 - 3 = 19.
#ASSERT `s 47(4) the additional pension in pounds` 22 3 EQUALS 19
-- (3): the relevant amount is the additional pension less any reduction under section 46 of the Pensions Act. 20 - 4.5 = 15.5.
#ASSERT `s 47(3) the relevant amount in pounds` 20 4.5 EQUALS 15.5
#ASSERT `s 47(3) the relevant amount in pounds` 20 0 EQUALS 20
-- (2): the relevant amount is deducted from the increase, and there is an increase only if a balance remains.
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the increase after the deduction in pounds` 10 TRUE 7 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the increase after the deduction in pounds` 10 TRUE 10 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the increase after the deduction in pounds` 10 TRUE 12 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the increase after the deduction in pounds` 10 FALSE 12 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the increase after the deduction in pounds` 10 TRUE 0 EQUALS 10
-- (5): the rate in force from time to time.
#ASSERT `s 47(5) the rate of the age addition in pounds` (JUST 4.5) EQUALS JUST 4.5
#ASSERT `s 47(5) the rate of the age addition in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 48: use of former spouse's contributions`

-- (4): a relevant relationship is a marriage or civil partnership.
#ASSERT `s 48(4) the relationship is a relevant relationship` `s 48(4) a marriage`
#ASSERT `s 48(4) the relationship is a relevant relationship` `s 48(4) a civil partnership`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 48(4) the relationship is a relevant relationship` `s 48(4) a relationship of another kind`))
-- (3): only the last relevant relationship.
#ASSERT `s 48(3) the relationship is not excluded by subsection (3)` TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 48(3) the relationship is not excluded by subsection (3)` FALSE))
-- (2): not for a person who attained pensionable age before 6 April 1979 if the termination also occurred before that date.
#ASSERT `s 48(2) subsection (1) is disapplied for the person` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1915) (Date 5 4 1979)) (Date 5 4 1979)
#ASSERT `s 48(2) subsection (1) is disapplied for the person` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1970)) (Date 1 1 1970)
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 48(2) subsection (1) is disapplied for the person` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1915) (Date 6 4 1979)) (Date 1 1 1970)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 48(2) subsection (1) is disapplied for the person` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1970)) (Date 6 4 1979)))
-- (2A): regulations may not treat contributions for times on or after 6 April 2016 as another person's; for earlier times the text is silent.
#ASSERT `s 48(2A) regulations under subsection (1) may provide for contributions in respect of the time to be treated as another person's` (Date 5 4 2016) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 48(2A) regulations under subsection (1) may provide for contributions in respect of the time to be treated as another person's` (Date 6 4 2016) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(2A) regulations under subsection (1) may provide for contributions in respect of the time to be treated as another person's` (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1): a person who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016, has been in a relevant relationship, and does not satisfy the conditions with their own contributions, may have the former spouse's treated as their own, for a Category A claim only.
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the former spouse's or civil partner's contributions may be treated as the person's own` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 5 4 2016)) TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the former spouse's or civil partner's contributions may be treated as the person's own` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 5 4 2016)) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the former spouse's or civil partner's contributions may be treated as the person's own` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 5 4 2016)) TRUE NOTHING TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the former spouse's or civil partner's contributions may be treated as the person's own` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 5 4 2016)) TRUE NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the former spouse's or civil partner's contributions may be treated as the person's own` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 5 4 2016)) TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the former spouse's or civil partner's contributions may be treated as the person's own` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 5 4 2016)) TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the former spouse's or civil partner's contributions may be treated as the person's own` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 6 4 2016)) TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the former spouse's or civil partner's contributions may be treated as the person's own` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 5 4 2016)) FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5): the four ways a civil partnership may end without being treated as terminated; any other way is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 48(5) the civil partnership is treated as having terminated` `s 48(5)(a) converted into a marriage under a conversion enactment named in paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(5) the civil partnership is treated as having terminated` `s 48(5)(b) changed into a marriage under the Marriage (Scotland) Act 1977` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(5) the civil partnership is treated as having terminated` `s 48(5)(c) changed into a marriage in accordance with provision made under section 10 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Scotland) Act 2014` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(5) the civil partnership is treated as having terminated` `s 48(5)(d) changed into a marriage under Part 5 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Scotland) Act 2014 and Civil Partnership Act 2004 (Consequential Provisions and Modifications) Order 2014` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(5) the civil partnership is treated as having terminated` `s 48(5) ended in some other way` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5), first version: conversion only.
#ASSERT `s 48(5) first version: the civil partnership is treated as having terminated by reason of the conversion` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(5) first version: the civil partnership is treated as having terminated by reason of the conversion` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6): a marriage converted into a civil partnership.
#ASSERT `s 48(6) the marriage is treated as having terminated` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(6) the marriage is treated as having terminated` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 48A: Category B retirement pension for married person or civil partner`

-- (6): paragraph 5 where the spouse was born before 6 April 1945; otherwise paragraph 5A.
