-- (6): where the spouse or civil partner died under pensionable age, the tax year is the one in which they died.
#ASSERT (`s 48BB(6) the tax year taken as the tax year in which the pensioner attained pensionable age` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 1 1 2012)) (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE)'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 1999
#ASSERT (`s 48BB(6) the tax year taken as the tax year in which the pensioner attained pensionable age` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 1 1 2012)) (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE)'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2011
-- (7): where the spouse or civil partner dies after 5 October 2002 the pension is one half of what it would otherwise be.
#ASSERT `s 48BB(7) the weekly rate before any reduction under subsection (8) in pounds` 100 (Date 6 10 2002) EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 48BB(7) the weekly rate before any reduction under subsection (8) in pounds` 100 (Date 5 10 2002) EQUALS 100
-- (8): 7 per cent. for each year (a fraction counting as a year) by which the pensioner was under 55, at most ten times. 55 minus 54 completed years = 1 year; 100 x 7% x 1 = 7.
